unction that chains a slice of normalize functions in order. Per prd001 R4.1-R4.3.\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Implement file-state comparison for utilities whose primary output is a file (sponge, cp, mv). DiffTest must allow specifying expected file paths and content after execution. File content is compared byte-for-byte with divergence reported in the same format as stdout divergence. Per prd001 R5.1-R5.2.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"RunDiffTests signature is RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary string, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) per prd001 AC1. This is the sole public entry point for cmd/ test files.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"DiffTest.Normalize is a []func([]byte) []byte slice applied in order per prd001 R4.3. When nil or empty, no normalization is applied. This replaces a single Normalize field with a composable slice.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Binary execution timeout uses context.WithTimeout with a default of 10 seconds per prd001 R2.3. The timeout applies independently to each binary invocation.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Each DiffTest runs as t.Run(testName, func(t *testing.T) { ... }) per prd001 R3.6, where testName is a field on DiffTest so individual failures are identifiable in go test output.\"\n      - id: D5\n        text: \"When no working directory is specified, both binaries run in a per-test temporary directory created via t.TempDir() per prd001 R2.5.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"DiffTest struct exists in pkg/testutils/difftest.go with all fields specified by prd001 R1.1-R1.4: Args, Stdin, Env, Name, Normalize, WorkDir, and file expectation fields.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests) is callable from a cmd/ test file with a []DiffTest slice and no other setup, per prd001 AC1.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Both binaries are executed with identical args, stdin, and environment. Stdout, stderr,